WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.600
This programme contains
some strong language

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.056
I have decided to declare a state of emergency.
The Prime Minister has issued a statement.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.440
A foreign power is attempting to subvert

4
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.840
our democracy and our elections

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.080
and that power is Russia.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.960
Following the attack on the UK's
political institutions and telecoms.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.480
Russian FSB hackers are being blamed.

8
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.840
This constitutes the cyber equivalent

9
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.640
of an armed attack
on the United Kingdom.

10
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.120
An act of war.

11
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.280
It is vital that we do not react
as expected now.

12
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.760
We need to hit back in a language
they understand.

13
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.080
It was the FSB coder Vadim Trusov
you met in Harrogate. wasn't it?

14
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.560
Yes.

15
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.360
Have you had any more
contact with him?

16
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.320
I understand you were
at college together.

17
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.920
Stage three of the Russian attack
was a data scrape.

18
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.440
All our own and the NSA's most
confidential material stolen.

19
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.960
As of 20:00 hours today. Eastern Time.

20
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.680
the NSA's intelligence sharing
arrangement with the UK is withdrawn

21
00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.640
for the foreseeable future.

22
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.440
JSS is showing Russian aircraft
entering our airspace.

23
00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.720
It is possible we are under attack.

24
00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.200
I'm sending you something now -
two things.

25
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.840
You can use them to trade with
the Americans to bring them back in.

26
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.160
As soon as it happens.
Putin will back down.

27
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.880
I put my life in your hands now. OK?

28
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.120
If they find out I told you this.
they will kill me.

29
00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.760
RAF squadrons are airborne.

30
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.880
They have a fix on
the unidentified aircraft.

31
00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.200
The Prime Minister is waiting for me.

32
00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.760
He's with the Chief of Staff.

33
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.240
I will be advising him to order
an immediate retaliatory attack

34
00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.200
on the Russian military base
in Kaliningrad.

35
00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.040
It's a provocation.

36
00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.080
I agree. A squadron of Russian
aircraft over the UK

37
00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.680
is a provocation.

38
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.480
An intolerable one.

39
00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.240
Vadim Trusov confirmed
that the Russians' intentions

40
00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.240
was to isolate us and then
provoke us into an act of war.

41
00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.600
If any of these aircraft exist at all.

42
00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.920
if they're Russian drones or missiles.

43
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.440
they want us to fire on them.

44
00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.200
We are playing their game.

45
00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.240
Sorry. how could they fake this?

46
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.040
Hacking Air Traffic Control.
faking air attacks.

47
00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.360
it's entirely in keeping with their MO.

48
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.960
No. we cannot take the risk.

49
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.120
We cannot do this without the
Americans being back on board!

50
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.240
Defence Secretary. we have no doubt
the material Vadim Trusov

51
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.600
leaked to us will encourage
the Americans

52
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.280
to renew military and intelligence
alliances with us.

53
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.960
Putin will back down.

54
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.480
The director of the NSA. General
Perez. has confirmed in writing

55
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:44.120
that all intelligence and military
alliances with the US are suspended.

56
00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.720
Perez hasn't seen the leaked material.

57
00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.080
The Prime Minister has tried
the President.

58
00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.240
He's at Camp David incommunicado
for the Middle East talks.

59
00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.880
RAF squadrons are minutes away
from intercep...

60
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.320
Try and get him to stop
declaring war on Russia

61
00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.600
for the next five minutes.
..Russian aircraft.

62
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.240
Sally.Encryption.

63
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.240
They've managed to reset the
nuclear codes. Some good news.

64
00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.240
OK. send that to the Defence Secretary

65
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.640
and then get me Michaela Jones on a
call in my office. now! Of course.

66
00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:17.480
Max. we need something to get
the Americans back on board.

67
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.200
This Russian exploit you found
in the Trusov material...

68
00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.880
Phil found it. actually.

69
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.440
It's malware breaching
the President's personal

70
00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.280
and domestic security.

71
00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.240
White House CCTV. everything.

72
00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.040
It's pretty ballsy.

73
00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.480
You can say that again.
Prep a secure link.

74
00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.840
Michaela's on the screen. Thank you.

75
00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:53.560
Michaela? Dan. Touched you've
taken the time out to call.

76
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.680
Something up? You could say that. yes.

77
00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:58.400
What's this about. Dan?

78
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.200
It's about not seeing 80 years
of intelligence sharing

79
00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.920
and collaboration go down the pan.

80
00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.960
I'm going to send you something

81
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.920
and I really need you to get Perez
to join a call for me.

82
00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.720
OK. Leave it with me.

83
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:15.160
Thank you. I owe you one. I've got to go.

84
00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.040
Max. send that exploit over secure link

85
00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.960
to Michaela Jones at the NSA.
please. Yeah. on it.

86
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.320
I need to talk to you. If it's
about Vadim. I will talk to MI6.

87
00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.720
but right now... It's not.
It's something else.

88
00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:40.360
I should have said earlier.
but with everything going on.

89
00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.720
and I had to check.

90
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.560
Danny. I've just put General Perez
through to the comms room.

91
00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.320
All right. thank you. Sally.
Just wait here for me. Saara. OK?

92
00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.680
I trust you're not going to ask
for our help.

93
00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.200
Those days are over.

94
00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:02.680
Danny. Yeah...

95
00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.000
Thank you for taking the call. sir.

96
00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.680
Trusov leaked terabytes
of the FSB's cyber capabilities

97
00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.480
and top secret data.

98
00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.000
At a conservative estimate.
it will set the FSB back years.

99
00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.640
losing this stuff.

100
00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:20.200
Now. Michaela Jones is making
one particular cyber exploit

101
00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.960
available to you now.

102
00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.120
We need you to convey this
to the President.

103
00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.240
In return. we need the re-establishment

104
00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.600
of all intelligence sharing agreements

105
00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.920
and for the President to tell the Russians

106
00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.960
to withdraw from our airspace.

107
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.320
We need this done immediately
or this war becomes real.

108
00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:41.720
What did you send him?

109
00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.520
Russian malware targeting
the President's own family.

110
00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.240
Thank you. We're on this now.

111
00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:51.640
You'll be hearing from us.
Please hold fire until you do.

112
00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.920
I hope this works.

113
00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.240
Defence Secretary...

114
00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.240
if I can take this opportunity.

115
00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.040
even if the special relationship
is indeed back up and running.

116
00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.480
we really need to be thinking
about next steps.

117
00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:12.040
Maybe not the time... How do we fix this?

118
00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:15.200
It's a huge clean up job
and my staff are on their knees

119
00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.120
after the last fortnight. Danny!

120
00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.920
The truth is. we are
desperately low on numbers

121
00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.720
of sufficiently skilled staff. sir.

122
00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:25.200
I can't overstate the importance
of us being ready

123
00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:27.640
should this happen again.
Last time I checked.

124
00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:30.240
GCHQ came under
the Foreign Secretary's authority.

125
00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:32.600
Well. since Elizabeth Kahn's resignation.

126
00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.640
there currently is no Foreign Secretary.

127
00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.240
Well. I will ask the Prime Minister
to bring it up with

128
00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:40.040
whomever he sees fit to appoint
to that august office.

129
00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.480
Shit.

130
00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.160
Christ. they're almost over London.

131
00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.120
I'm ordering a strike on Kaliningrad.

132
00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.200
Wait. Sir. if they're fake and we attack.

133
00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.000
we are the aggressor.

134
00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.480
It was fake.

135
00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.080
It was fake all along.
They're playing with us.

136
00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.520
Lucky.

137
00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.040
I don't like relying on luck.

138
00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.160
Gentlemen.

139
00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.640
Maybe the Americans are helping
after all.

140
00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.880
Danny. Yeah?

141
00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.960
With Marston.
you've got to pick your moment.

142
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.560
We have a Cobra meeting
in London tomorrow morning.

143
00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.280
We can discuss next steps
with them then.

144
00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.040
Understood.

145
00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:18.240
I'm sorry. Saara. What was it?

146
00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.240
When we shut off the data scrape.
our sandbox computer.

147
00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:24.040
which the Russian malware
broke out of... What about it?

148
00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:27.200
What am I looking at?

149
00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.720
Yes. James.

150
00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.880
Good. good. Well. that's...
That's excellent news.

151
00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.880
Yes. Thank you so much.

152
00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.880
Jesus Christ.

153
00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.680
Charlie. I need you up in my office ASAP.

154
00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.200
Yes. ASAP.

155
00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.840
Thank you. buddy.

156
00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.160
Danny.

157
00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.920
Well. the President called Putin.

158
00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:56.720
Cease all action against the UK
or expect the full force

159
00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.160
of a combined NATO response
under Article 5.

160
00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.200
Putin has backed down.

161
00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.800
For now.

162
00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:09.240
That's good. David. No. that's excellent.

163
00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:12.160
and you're the one that got
the Americans back in the game...

164
00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:14.800
so what's wrong?

165
00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.080
I've had to call in Charlie Francis.

166
00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.440
OK.

167
00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:21.880
Saara.

168
00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.960
Come into my office.

169
00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.640
So. what's going on. Danny?

170
00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.400
Charlie. You're lucky you caught me.
I was just heading off.

171
00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.440
Or maybe not so lucky.

172
00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:46.040
Something tells me I'm
not getting home tonight.

173
00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.800
Saara. you know Charlie Francis.
Head of Security.

174
00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:53.160
Saara has something for us. Charlie.
And I'm afraid it is not good.

175
00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:54.960
How not good? For you to determine.

176
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.160
but we think it could
be potentially disastrous.

177
00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.560
Right. It's how the Russian

178
00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.920
malware got into our systems
in the first place.

179
00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:05.360
If I understood correctly.
it was through a sandbox computer.

180
00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.040
They knew we'd put the malware
in there to analyse it.

181
00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:10.400
Yeah. but it could only
break out if it knew ahead

182
00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.120
of time which sandbox
it was going to be put into.

183
00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:17.120
OK. The Media Access Control.
The Mac address.

184
00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:21.200
It's a 12 digit alphanumeric
identifier unique to each computer.

185
00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.600
It was written into the third
stage Russian malware code.

186
00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.920
Meaning? The writers of the code

187
00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.480
had to have it
before it ever arrived at GCHQ.

188
00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.120
It's offline. high side.

189
00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.760
So the only way they could
have known is... A CI.

190
00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:38.680
In old money. a mole.

191
00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:49.760
One of us.

192
00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.320
Reports overnight
of further cyber attacks

193
00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.720
on the UK by Russia.

194
00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.880
Surely this begs the
question. are we safe?

195
00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.640
Do you think the Government
is doing enough

196
00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.000
to respond to these attacks?
What should.

197
00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.960
Prime Minister Andrew Makinde do
in the face of Putin's aggression?

198
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.000
Give us a call.

199
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.160
Hello. stranger.

200
00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.560
Barbara. my love.

201
00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.480
Charlie told me you didn't go
to France like we agreed.

202
00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.640
Well. if the world's going to end...

203
00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.200
I'd quite like to be with you.

204
00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:13.360
I'm glad you didn't go.

205
00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.560
It was a false alarm.

206
00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.080
Bad?

207
00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:39.440
How are the boys? Fine.

208
00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:40.480
Oblivious.

209
00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:43.960
It's one benefit of teenage hormones.

210
00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:55.360
What was it? You know I can't tell you.

211
00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:58.800
Three guesses.

212
00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.840
I'm tired. Barbara. You wanted us
packed off to France

213
00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.176
and I'm not even allowed to guess

214
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:08.640
the reason why? It was
Russia. wasn't it?

215
00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:12.040
Well. the news made that quite clear.

216
00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.800
So guess one.

217
00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:20.600
They said there was a data breach.

218
00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:23.600
You can speculate all you like.
but I couldn't possibly say.

219
00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.680
Shit! How?

220
00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.680
Information possessed by...
..Virtue of your position.

221
00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:42.120
Three and out. But you will
tell me. Danny Patrick.

222
00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:45.400
I insist you tell me.

223
00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:48.720
Damn your insistence. Agent Napier.

224
00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.080
You'll never get it out of me.

225
00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.160
Don't you ever dream
of just jacking it all in?

226
00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:07.720
Dream. perhaps. But...

227
00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.160
if everyone thought like that...

228
00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.440
There'd be no-one left to save the world.

229
00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:39.080
Er. stay. I should at least say hi.

230
00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.720
They'll survive.

231
00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.000
I'll go and wake them up.
I'll do the drop before work.

232
00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.120
Right.

233
00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.120
Right. Come on.

234
00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.600
Mr Marston.

235
00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:21.520
how is it potential Russian
aircraft were allowed

236
00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:23.000
to fly so near to London?

237
00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:26.400
We knew all along
the attack was probably a fake.

238
00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:29.080
If we responded.
we would have been the aggressor.

239
00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:32.120
Cyber warfare is notoriously escalatory.

240
00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:34.480
and this is just the latest in a string

241
00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:37.840
of unacceptable Russian
provocations. That they could gain

242
00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.560
access to our radar systems is...

243
00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:43.560
of course. of serious concern.
and the PM and I are very clear

244
00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:46.760
that our cyber defences
must be strengthened.

245
00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.040
There's only so long we can
keep this to ourselves.

246
00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.160
Danny and I are to brief

247
00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.040
the Prime Minister and security directors.

248
00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:55.080
We should inform them about our mole.

249
00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:56.896
If we inform them.
then they're going to bring

250
00:16:56.920 --> 00:17:00.040
in external investigators
and work will be disrupted.

251
00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.120
And the mole will run to ground.

252
00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:05.240
We have a duty. We have a duty
to fix our entire network

253
00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:08.840
after this attack and find the
mole as quickly as possible.

254
00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:12.280
